## Breaking change addressed (v4.33 -> v4.34)
`Finset.prod_le_one` / `Finset.prod_le_prod` in v4.34 require
`[MulLeftMono N]` (CovariantClass N N (·*·) (·≤·)), which cannot be synthesized
for ℝ (fails for negative multipliers). All 15 call sites in Erdos42.lean were
rewritten to the nonneg variants `Finset.prod_le_one₀` / `Finset.prod_le_prod₀`
from Mathlib/Algebra/Order/BigOperators/GroupWithZero/Finset.lean, which take an
explicit `∀ i ∈ s, 0 ≤ f i` argument and only require
`[CommMonoidWithZero R] [Preorder R] [ZeroLEOneClass R] [PosMulMono R]`
(all satisfied by ℝ). No mathematical content changed; the added hypotheses are
norm/abs nonnegativity and existing pointwise nonnegativity facts already in
context.

